Lesson 9: MCP — discover tools at runtime

Tools no longer have to be hardcoded. Model Context Protocol lets
the agent connect to external servers and fetch tool definitions on
the fly. Local tools and remote MCP tools share one interface, so
the agent loop doesn't care which is which.

Try: "What's happening in tech today?" (uses Tavily search via MCP).
Requires TAVILY_API_KEY in .env.
